    <div class="oga-container-narrow">
      <div class="oga-section-header oga-center"><span class="oga-section-label">Frequently Asked</span><h2>Ogawa Massage Chair FAQ</h2></div>
      <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--oga-border)">
        <div class="oga-faq-item"><div class="oga-faq-q" onclick="ogaToggleFaq(this)"><h3>How much does the Ogawa Master Drive Duo cost?</h3><svg class="oga-faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M19 13h-6v6h-2v-6H5v-2h6V5h2v6h6v2z"/></svg></div><div class="oga-faq-a"><p>The Ogawa Master Drive Duo is currently priced at <strong>$9,399</strong> at House of Massage Chairs (compare at $15,999 MSRP — saving of $6,600). Available in Black/Burgundy, Black/Champagne, and Platinum/Platinum. Affirm financing available.</p></div></div>
        <div class="oga-faq-item"><div class="oga-faq-q" onclick="ogaToggleFaq(this)"><h3>How much does the Ogawa Active XL 3D cost?</h3><svg class="oga-faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M19 13h-6v6h-2v-6H5v-2h6V5h2v6h6v2z"/></svg></div><div class="oga-faq-a"><p>The Ogawa Active XL 3D is currently priced at <strong>$3,299</strong> at House of Massage Chairs (compare at $5,999 MSRP — saving of $2,700). Available in Black, Gun Metal/Brown, Gun Metal/Ivory, and Green/Cappuccino.</p></div></div>
        <div class="oga-faq-item"><div class="oga-faq-q" onclick="ogaToggleFaq(this)"><h3>What is the difference between the Master Drive Duo and Active XL 3D?</h3><svg class="oga-faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M19 13h-6v6h-2v-6H5v-2h6V5h2v6h6v2z"/></svg></div><div class="oga-faq-a"><p>The Master Drive Duo ($9,399) uses dual independent mechanisms — a 4D roller and a 3D roller working simultaneously — plus AI Chair Doctor biometric sensing, 25 auto programs, 32 airbags. The Active XL 3D ($3,299) uses a single 3D IntelliGlide mechanism on an L-Curve SL-Track, with a wider 23″ seat, 30 airbags, triple-zone heat, foot rollers, and height range to 6'4″.</p></div></div>
        <div class="oga-faq-item"><div class="oga-faq-q" onclick="ogaToggleFaq(this)"><h3>What is the Ogawa Master Drive Duo AI Chair Doctor?</h3><svg class="oga-faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M19 13h-6v6h-2v-6H5v-2h6V5h2v6h6v2z"/></svg></div><div class="oga-faq-a"><p>AI Chair Doctor uses built-in biometric sensors — heart rate, galvanic skin response (GSR), and blood oxygen (SpO2) — to read your real-time physiological state and adapt the massage accordingly. It is a dynamic adaptation system using actual biometric data, not a standard body-height scan.</p></div></div>
        <div class="oga-faq-item"><div class="oga-faq-q" onclick="ogaToggleFaq(this)"><h3>Which Ogawa chair fits taller or wider buyers?</h3><svg class="oga-faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M19 13h-6v6h-2v-6H5v-2h6V5h2v6h6v2z"/></svg></div><div class="oga-faq-a"><p>The Ogawa Active XL 3D accommodates 5'0″–6'4″ at 320 lbs, with a 23-inch seat and shoulder width. The Master Drive Duo tops at 6'1″ with a 21.3-inch seat. If you are 6'2″+ or have wider shoulders, the Active XL 3D is the correct Ogawa.</p></div></div>
        <div class="oga-faq-item"><div class="oga-faq-q" onclick="ogaToggleFaq(this)"><h3>Can I try Ogawa massage chairs before buying?</h3><svg class="oga-faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M19 13h-6v6h-2v-6H5v-2h6V5h2v6h6v2z"/></svg></div><div class="oga-faq-a"><p>Yes — both models are available at our San Jose showroom (Westfield Oakridge Mall, 925 Blossom Hill Road) and Pleasanton (Stoneridge Shopping Center, 1116 Stoneridge Mall Rd). Book at <a href="{{ shop.url }}/pages/our-store">houseofmassagechairs.com/pages/our-store</a></p></div></div>
        <div class="oga-faq-item"><div class="oga-faq-q" onclick="ogaToggleFaq(this)"><h3>What are the Ogawa Master Drive Duo dimensions?</h3><svg class="oga-faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M19 13h-6v6h-2v-6H5v-2h6V5h2v6h6v2z"/></svg></div><div class="oga-faq-a"><p>Upright: 63.6″ × 31.9″ × 50″. Reclined: 73.7″ × 31.9″ × 41.5″. Seat width 21.3″. Wall clearance 1 inch. Chair weight 273.6 lbs. Weight capacity 320 lbs.</p></div></div>
        <div class="oga-faq-item"><div class="oga-faq-q" onclick="ogaToggleFaq(this)"><h3>What are the Ogawa Active XL 3D dimensions?</h3><svg class="oga-faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M19 13h-6v6h-2v-6H5v-2h6V5h2v6h6v2z"/></svg></div><div class="oga-faq-a"><p>Upright: 60.6″ × 30″ × 46.8″. Reclined: 73.6″ × 30″ × 35″. Seat width 23″. Shoulder width 23″. Net weight 202.8 lbs. Weight capacity 320 lbs. Zero wall recline.</p></div></div>
        <div class="oga-faq-item"><div class="oga-faq-q" onclick="ogaToggleFaq(this)"><h3>Are Ogawa massage chairs good?</h3><svg class="oga-faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M19 13h-6v6h-2v-6H5v-2h6V5h2v6h6v2z"/></svg></div><div class="oga-faq-a"><p>Yes — Ogawa chairs are consistently well-regarded for their balanced massage feel, build quality, and purposeful design. The Master Drive Duo's simultaneous dual-mechanism coverage is a verified technical differentiator. The Active XL 3D's roomier fit and accessible pricing are well-received by buyers who have found competitive chairs too narrow or too expensive.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

